        "original_id": "fe82b2c9-a14e-5a6d-b55c-e52a760bf1a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Joy Formidable, Sixpence None the Richer\n- People: Leigh Nash\n- Products: A Heavy Abacus, The Big Roar, Wishing for This\n- Places: North Wales, London, England, New Braunfels, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Topics: alternative rock, Christian rock, indie pop\n\nFacts:\n- The Joy Formidable is a Welsh alternative rock band that was formed in 2007 in North Wales and is currently based in London, England.\n- Sixpence None the Richer, also known as Sixpence, is an American alternative Christian rock band that formed in New Braunfels, Texas, and later settled in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- \"A Heavy Abacus\" was released in July 2011 as the fifth and final single from The Joy Formidable's debut album \"The Big Roar.\"\n- Wishing for This is a Christmas EP by Leigh Nash, who is an alternative rock and indie pop artist and a member of Sixpence None the Richer.",
